---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import Reveal from '../components/Reveal.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { company } from '../data/site';

/**
 * Privacy policy.
 *
 * URL deliberately matches the original site: /english-privacy-policy. The
 * "english-" prefix is odd but it is the live URL, so it is preserved rather
 * than tidied — changing it would break inbound links and search results.
 *
 * The original page was an UNEDITED Wix template describing what a privacy
 * policy should generally contain, rather than what Urjapod actually does
 * with data. This page instead describes THIS build accurately:
 *   - static site, no analytics, no tracking, no cookies set by us
 *   - the contact form currently opens the visitor's own mail client
 *   - no data reaches a server we control until FORM_ENDPOINT is configured
 *
 * TODO(confirm): this is a plain-language description of actual data
 * handling, NOT legal advice, and it has not been reviewed by a lawyer. Have
 * it reviewed before launch — particularly for India's Digital Personal Data
 * Protection Act, 2023, and for GDPR if you market into the EU.
 *
 * TODO(confirm): if you add analytics, a chat widget, embedded maps, or wire
 * up a contact-form backend, this page MUST be updated — each of those
 * introduces data collection that the text below currently says does not
 * happen.
 */
const lastUpdated = 'August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Urjapod Energy handles personal information collected through this website, what we collect, why, and how to contact us about it."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy policy"
    lead="What this website collects, why, and what we do with it. In short: this is a static site with no tracking, and the only personal information we hold is what you choose to send us."
  />

  <Section width="narrow">
    <Reveal>
      <div
        class="mb-10 flex gap-3 rounded-panel border border-ink-200 bg-ink-100 p-5"
      >
        <Icon name="clock" class="mt-0.5 size-5 shrink-0 text-ink-600" />
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-700">
          <strong class="font-semibold text-ink-900">Draft — needs legal review.</strong>
          This describes how the site actually behaves today, but it has not
          been reviewed by a lawyer and is not legal advice. Have it checked
          against India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 before
          launch, and update it if you add analytics or a contact-form backend.
        </p>
      </div>

      <Prose>
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          This website is operated by <strong>{company.legalName}</strong>
          (CIN {company.cin}), {company.address.line1},
          {' '}{company.address.line2}, {company.address.city},
          {' '}{company.address.state} {company.address.postcode}, India.
        </p>
        <p>
          For any question about this policy or about your personal
          information, contact
          {' '}<a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Information you send us.</strong> If you contact us — through
          the form on our contact page, by email, or by phone — we receive
          whatever you choose to tell us. Typically that is your name, company,
          email address, phone number and details of the project you are asking
          about.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> We do not run
          analytics, advertising or tracking software on this site. We do not
          set cookies. There are no third-party scripts, embedded fonts,
          trackers or social widgets — every file the site loads is served from
          our own domain.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our hosting provider may keep standard server logs, which can include
          IP addresses and browser details, for security and reliability. That
          is ordinary infrastructure logging, not something we use to profile
          visitors.
        </p>

        <h2>How the contact form works</h2>
        <p>
          The contact form does not currently send anything to us directly.
          When you submit it, it opens your own email application with the
          message prepared, and nothing is sent until you send it yourself. In
          other words, your enquiry reaches us as an ordinary email, and no
          form data passes through any third-party service.
        </p>

        <h2>Why we use it, and on what basis</h2>
        <p>
          We use the information you send us for one purpose: to reply to your
          enquiry and, if it leads somewhere, to carry out the resulting
          business relationship — quoting, designing, supplying, commissioning
          or maintaining an energy storage system.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not sell your information, we do not share it with anyone for
          marketing, and we will not add you to a mailing list because you
          contacted us about a project.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>
          We do not share your personal information with third parties, except:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            our email provider, which necessarily processes messages sent to
            us;
          </li>
          <li>
            professional advisers, or where we are required to disclose
            information by law or by a competent authority.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Enquiries are kept only as long as there is a reason to: while we are
          in conversation with you, and afterwards for as long as needed for
          the resulting contract and for our legal and tax obligations. If an
          enquiry does not lead anywhere, we delete it once it is clearly no
          longer relevant.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us to confirm what personal information we hold about
          you, to correct it if it is wrong, or to delete it. You can also ask
          us to stop using it. Email
          {' '}<a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a> and we
          will respond.
        </p>
        <p>
          Depending on where you live, you may also have the right to complain
          to a data protection authority.
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          This site is served over HTTPS. We take reasonable measures to
          protect the information you send us, though no method of transmission
          over the internet is completely secure.
        </p>

        <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
        <p>
          This site links to external pages, such as our LinkedIn profile. We
          are not responsible for the privacy practices of sites we do not
          operate, and we would encourage you to read their policies.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we change how this site handles personal information — for
          example by adding analytics or a form backend — we will update this
          page. It was last reviewed in {lastUpdated}.
        </p>
      </Prose>
    </Reveal>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
